Changes made in this fork (Apache License 2.0, section 4(b)):

Modified upstream files (each carries a "Modified by AmagiLabs" header):
  src/extensions_ref/tiny_llm_ext_ref/__init__.py
      Adds an opt-in switch: with TINY_LLM_BACKEND=cuda the reference extension's kernels are
      loaded from src/tiny_llm_cuda_kernels instead of the compiled Metal library. Without the
      variable the file behaves as upstream.
  README.md
      Replaced with this fork's README. The upstream README is kept verbatim as README.upstream.md.

New files (each carries an AmagiLabs copyright header):
  NOTICE
  README.upstream.md          (upstream README.md, moved, content unchanged)
  requirements-cuda.txt
  docs/cuda/DESIGN.md
  src/tiny_llm_cuda_kernels/  (__init__.py, common.py, week2.py, quantized.py, matrix.py,
                               paged.py, attention.py, flash.py, week3_patch.py, ext_shim.py)
      CUDA ports, written with mlx.core.fast.cuda_kernel, of the Metal kernels in
      src/extensions_ref/src. week3_patch.py also contains code adapted from
      src/tiny_llm_ref/qwen3_week3.py and src/tiny_llm_ref/paged_kv_cache.py, applied at import
      time when the CUDA backend is enabled; the upstream files themselves are not edited.
